{"name":"Bright and Breezy","hex":"#b5ddeb","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bright","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Emitting much light; visually dazzling; luminous, lucent, radiant.","Of light: brilliant, intense."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Brightness, glow.\n\n Glory, splendour.","Brightness, glow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bright"},{"term":"and","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ansus."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["As a coordinating conjunction; expressing two elements to be taken together or in addition to each other.\nUsed simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\nSimply connecting two clauses or sentences. \n\nIntroducing a clause or sentence which follows on in time or consequence from the first.","Used simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/and"},{"term":"breezy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["With a breeze blowing, with a lively wind, pleasantly windy.","With a cheerful, casual, lively and light-hearted manner."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young woman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breezy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bright and Breezy","blocks":[{"text":"Bright and Breezy is an album by jazz pianist Red Garland and his trio, recorded in 1961 and released on Jazzland as JLP 48. Sam Jones had been the trio's bassist for two years. Art Taylor, who had played drums in the Red Garland Trio since 1956, was replaced by Charlie Persip in 1960. This was the first of four sessions by Garland for the Riverside subsidiary label, that were recorded at the Plaza Sound Studios by Orrin Keepnews. In October 1962 he would record a last session for his former label Prestige before taking a hiatus of nearly ten years."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fc/Bright_%26_Breezy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bright_and_Breezy"},{"title":"Breezy","blocks":[{"text":"Breezy is a 1973 American romantic drama film directed by Clint Eastwood, produced by Robert Daley, and written by Jo Heims. The film stars William Holden and Kay Lenz, with Roger C. Carmel, Marj Dusay, and Joan Hotchkis in supporting roles. It is the third film directed by Eastwood and the first without him starring in it."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Breezyfilmposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breezy"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"bright":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/be/En-us-bright.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/be/En-us-bright.ogg/En-us-bright.ogg.mp3"}],"and":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/26/En-us-and.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/26/En-us-and.ogg/En-us-and.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/35/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Pvanp7-and_%28stressed%29.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/35/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Pvanp7-and_%28stressed%29.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Pvanp7-and_%28stressed%29.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/35/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Pvanp7-and_%28stressed%29.wav/LL-Q1860_%2